  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q6-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "6",
    "prompt": "The ratio of male to female voters in an election was $4:3$. Had 8 fewer men and 14 fewer women voted, the ratio would have been $2:1$. Find the total number of votes cast.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "70 votes.\n\nForm equations from the two ratios and solve by substitution.",
      "worked": "Let $x$ and $y$ be the original numbers of male and female voters respectively.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3x&=4y &&(1)\\\\x-8&=2(y-14) &&(2)\\\\x-8&=2y-28\\\\x&=2y-20\\end{align*}$$\n\nSubstitute into (1).\n\n$$\\begin{align*}3(2y-20)&=4y\\\\6y-60&=4y\\\\2y&=60\\\\y&=30\\\\x&=2(30)-20\\\\x&=40\\\\x+y&=40+30\\\\x+y&=70\\end{align*}$$\n\nTherefore, 70 votes were cast.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 124
  },
